NUMBERS.md §7 said 14/14 (4 + 2 + 1 + 4 + 2 + 1). Its own §5.12 and
PAPER.md (§7 'Sample size', line 1311; conclusion, line 1687) say 15,
with two hardcopy runs. gauntlet/RESULTS.md records both: the hardcopy
round (Codex, 5/5) and the gap-completion round's replication (Kimi,
6/6). So 4 + 2 + 1 + 4 + 2 + 2 = 15. The four-fifths bound still holds:
the one-sided 95% lower bound on 15/15 is 0.05^(1/15) = 0.82.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
